  "text": "Library | University of Cape Coast Skip to main content Academics Explore all programmes Programmes & Learning Academic Structure Student Resources Library Admissions Experience what UCC can offer you Apply Browse Programmes Announcements Applicants and Students Explore UCC Corporate Strategic Plan About the University Official Documents Governance Governance and Administration Executive Leadership Governance Bodies Academic Leadership Staff Directory Campus Our Campus Facilities Life at UCC Research UCC Scholar Publications & Conferences Research Support News & Media News Updates Trending News Events Videos University of Cape Coast Search Ctrl K Menu Ctrl M Home Home Navigate to Library Loading search… Site navigation menu University Information Library The University Library System comprises the Main Library, Faculty Libraries, Departmental Libraries and Hall Libraries. These are of varying sizes, content and service and are distributed across the campus. Staff and students of the University are allowed to use the library for reference and borrowing purposes. The Main Library, Sam Jonah Library, offers a diverse and innovative range of products and services to cater for the need of every user. The library subscribes to electronic resources through the Consortium of Academic and Research Libraries of Ghana (CALIGH). These are protected by publishers using a variety of authentication technologies to ensure that only authorised links can gain access to the full-text content. The library also provides hypertext links to websites which in turn give free access to full-text electronic documents, e journals and other free Internet resources. Corporate Strategic Plan UCC’s roadmap for innovation, global impact, and national development (2023–2027). Library Banking Bookshops Post Office Places of Worship Healthcare Network and Infrastructure Section Childcare facilities on UCC campus Share via social media or copy link Facebook Twitter LinkedIn WhatsApp Email Page Link Copy University of Cape Coast The #1 University in Ghana and West Africa Empowering minds, transforming lives, and\nbuilding the future through excellence in education and research. Get in Touch University of Cape Coast Cape Coast, Ghana +233 (03321) 32440 registrar@ucc.edu.gh Data protection: dataprotection@ucc.edu.gh Quick Links Programmes Web Services Forms Directory MyUCC University About UCC Announcements Events News Research Journals UCC Scholar Conferences Resources Library E-Learning Videos Connect With Us © 2026 University of Cape Coast. All rights reserved. Privacy Policy | Terms of Service | Cookie Policy | Accessibility | Cookie Settings | Your Data Cookies on this site We need some cookies to make the site work at all, and those are already set. Saying\nno to the rest costs you nothing — the site works exactly the same either way. Customise Beyond the cookies already set, we would like to measure which pages are read\nso we can decide what to fix. We will not set anything for that until you say\nyes. You can change your mind at any time from Cookie Settings in the footer. Strictly necessary — always on, no choice offered Keeps you signed in and lets forms be submitted safely. Nothing here follows\nyou to other websites. Analytics These tell us which pages people read, how they arrived, and where they give up, and we use that to decide what to fix. They are not used to advertise to you, and we do not sell what they collect. Behaviour analytics Set only while the site’s heatmap feature is switched on, which it is not by default. It records anonymised interaction — where on a page people click, how far they scroll — to show us which parts of a page are being missed. Every cookie named, and the companies behind them, are listed in the cookie policy . Reject all Accept all Save my choices",
